WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.770
Barbarian is full of some truly eye-popping
scares.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.770
Literally.

00:00:05.251 --> 00:00:09.950
Part of what makes "Barbarian" such a rollercoaster
of terror is how it keeps its answers in the

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.500
dark to let your mind simmer on the worst
possibilities.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:18.429
The moment Tess, played by Georgina Campbell,
arrives at the double-booked rental, her first

00:00:18.429 --> 00:00:24.029
discovery is learning somebody else is staying
in the house - Keith played by Bill Skarsgård.

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:27.509
She keeps her guard up but eventually softens
to the idea.

00:00:27.509 --> 00:00:32.239
One night Keith goes missing and Tess hears
his faint screaming coming from downstairs.

00:00:32.239 --> 00:00:37.040
Tess enters the dark basement and manages
to find a secret doorway by pulling on a rope

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.610
coming out of the wall.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:43.690
The doorway opens up to a pitch-black space
and makes your mind rattle with possibilities.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.552
"Nope."

00:00:46.945 --> 00:00:51.510
Tess works up the courage to enter and as
she travels into the dark space that's when

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.360
the stakes of the movie rise exponentially.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:58.760
Tess discovers a dingy and desolate hidden
side room for the first time, which truly

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.760
makes for a horrifying moment.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:05.620
The disgusting mattress, sleazy lighting,
and video camera make it feel like Tess is

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:11.240
walking into the setting of a snuff film,
which sadly isn't far from the truth.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:15.550
The twists and turns mount on top of each
other as the film plays on your assumptions.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:21.130
AJ, played by Justin Long, finds Frank's bedroom
where he discovers the snuff films Frank,

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:25.060
played by Richard Brake, recorded as he kidnapped
women throughout his life.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:30.820
The room Tess found earlier in the film serves
as both an immediate scare and a super terrifying

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.540
breadcrumb leading us to Frank's backstory.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.930
It's a story that began decades ago.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:40.330
The final discovery Tess makes is that the
Mother everyone has feared all this time is

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:42.879
also a victim of her father's abuse.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:47.720
The Mother is a constantly terrifying threat
throughout "Barbarian," but it's her initial

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:51.360
debut that's the most terrifying since it
comes out of nowhere.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.510
By the time the Mother enters the picture,
you're completely engaged with Tess and Keith's

00:01:55.510 --> 00:02:00.580
fun chemistry and their growing bond as well
as the intriguing mystery that's afoot.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:05.060
When she finally does arrive towards the end
of the first act, you're totally in the dark

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:10.636
about what's really going on and it makes
her shambling out of the shadows absolutely horrifying.

00:02:10.636 --> 00:02:16.340
Just as Tess and Keith reunite in a dark and
dingy tunnel, the Mother comes from the shadows

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:21.860
to deliver a terrifying fright and perform
a shocking and bloody kill on Keith by repeatedly

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.930
bashing his head against a wall.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:28.240
It's a moment where the horrors of "Barbarian"
really come out to play and it's an incredibly

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:33.790
memorable way to hook horror fans through
a fantastic reveal of a terrifying horror antagonist.

00:02:34.011 --> 00:02:38.630
AJ is such a clueless person, that when he
first enters the house, he mostly ignores

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.880
all the warning signs that things are off.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:44.970
He's so hopelessly dim that even when he finds
the secret room in the basement, he thinks

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:50.000
nothing of it and whips out the tape measure
to see if he can get more value out of the property.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.280
AJ unknowingly brings himself deeper into
trouble as he travels farther into the tunnels.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.971
Eventually, the Mother starts to toy with
AJ by messing with his tape measurer, even

00:02:59.971 --> 00:03:01.810
ripping it away from him.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:06.209
It's a great moment of comedy turning to horror
as it kicks off a wild chase sequence through

00:03:06.209 --> 00:03:10.590
the tunnels that leaves AJ trapped and reveals
Tess is still alive.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:15.209
Plus, the tape measure comes back later in
the film to nearly thwart Tess' escape and

00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:18.415
provide a good jump scare in an already-tense
moment.

00:03:18.743 --> 00:03:23.270
After AJ and Tess meet while being captured
by The Mother, you can't help but wonder what

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:29.090
she plans to do with these two, and the answer
is truly creepier than one's wildest imagination.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:33.440
Viewers quickly learn why the creature is
credited as "The Mother" as she tries to perform

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:37.740
motherly behavior on Tess and AJ to make them
like her children.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:42.810
However, given the Mother's grotesque look,
motherly duties have never looked so morbid.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.989
"You cannot get upset."

00:03:44.989 --> 00:03:50.129
The entire sequence is a total nail-biter
as Tess' survival instincts force her to blend

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:55.810
into the situation by reluctantly drinking
the baby bottle filled with the Mother's breast milk.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:04:00.370
It's a nasty moment that hits you right in
the gut, but it's ultimately a smart choice

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:03.150
given what happens to AJ when he refuses.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:07.349
It's tough not to be squirming in your seat
when the Mother drags AJ through the tunnels

00:04:07.349 --> 00:04:09.000
and breastfeeds him.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.980
Overall, "Barbarian" certainly makes you understand
why the Mother earns her name and it couldn't

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:17.399
be more disturbing, strange and heartbreaking.

00:04:17.844 --> 00:04:22.419
After both AJ and an injured Tess leave the
house, they are sheltered by Andre, played

00:04:22.419 --> 00:04:26.990
by Jaymes Butler, a local homeless man, who
allows them a moment of solace as the Mother

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:28.470
continues to look for them.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:33.690
It's here that Andre discloses the Mother's
gut-wrenching origins and tries to give AJ

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.960
and Tess a moment to catch their breath.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:40.620
But good moments don't last for long in "Barbarian,"
and with one little comment about his place

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.300
being safe, they end up being Andre's famous
last words.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.510
The sudden reappearance of the Mother results
in a great jump scare and not only kicks off

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:53.690
a thrilling final chase but delivers a truly
brutal kill as the Mother rips Andre's arm

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:56.080
off and beats him to death.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:01.020
"Barbarian" features some surprisingly gruesome
kills throughout and Andre's is no different.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:06.190
It's a bloody end to a character with good
intentions and a memorably terrifying moment

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:09.320
that breaks the calming atmosphere with sudden
terror.

00:05:09.736 --> 00:05:13.590
One of the earliest scares in "Barbarian"
comes when Tess and Keith are first in the

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:18.209
house together for the night and Keith has
a night terror that makes for an unnerving sequence.

00:05:18.209 --> 00:05:22.740
After Tess wakes up from someone or something
opening her door and making a creepy sound

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:27.479
while she is sleeping, she finds that Keith
is wrestling and moaning on the couch.

00:05:27.479 --> 00:05:32.310
What follows is an absolutely nerve-racking
sequence showing Tess walking towards Keith

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.770
as he has some serious night terrors.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:38.820
Tess approaching Keith is purely thrilling
and the growing sounds of Keith's cries of

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.440
terror increase the tension immensely.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:45.850
The jump scare that comes from Keith suddenly
waking up delivers a perfect jolt to viewers

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:49.230
and acts as a great end stinger to a scary
sequence.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:53.150
It all ends with some good laughs with the
awkward exchange between Tess and Keith, but

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:57.860
it's an unforgettably tense moment early in
the film that sets the tone perfectly and

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:59.500
instills some good chills.

00:06:00.078 --> 00:06:01.467
"No, no, no, wait!"

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:05.830
Even though we know that AJ is basically the
worst person ever as it becomes clear that

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:10.080
he's guilty of sexual assault, Tess doesn't
know that and does everything in her power

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.610
to try and save him.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:16.100
After Tess initially escapes, she goes back
into the house to traverse the dark corridors

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.090
and eventually makes her way back to the Mother's
room.

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:23.350
Soon after, she notices a light peeking out
through the darkness, and with one little

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:27.180
response, she finds herself on the ground
with a bullet in her gut.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:32.130
What Tess didn't realize is that AJ was able
to get a pistol from Frank, and is now nervously

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:35.530
going through the tunnels still believing
that the Mother is hiding somewhere.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:40.680
Thus, when he sees a shadowy figure standing
just a short distance away, he doesn't hesitate

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:41.949
to fire.

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:44.880
Only after he fires does he learn it was Tess
standing there.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.760
The entire sequence is thrilling.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:51.140
The build-up to Tess returning into the house
is incredibly tense, and the moment she sees

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:55.819
the light of AJ's phone leaves you silent
and then instantly frightened by the well-timed

00:06:55.819 --> 00:06:57.140
jump scare of the gunshot.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:01.210
You're left even more scared afterward as
Tess clings on as she bleeds for the rest

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.210
of the film.

00:07:02.512 --> 00:07:06.610
Just as all hope seems lost for Tess after
the cops don't believe her and she's once

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:10.680
again left on her own, she decides to take
the Mother head-on with the help of something

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.120
mentioned by Andre.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:16.530
Amongst his ramblings, Andre mentions that
the Mother only comes out at night and with

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:20.669
that knowledge, Tess manages to ram her car
into the Mother when she appears, pinning

00:07:20.669 --> 00:07:24.350
her against the house and in the process breaking
the windshield.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:28.370
The anticipation leading up to the moment
the Mother rises from the small basement window

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:32.060
is killer and when she does appear it's through
a sudden scare.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:36.259
It's incredibly creepy to watch her slowly
crawl out of the tiny window hole and there

00:07:36.259 --> 00:07:40.940
is something satisfying about Tess finally
taking action against the Mother to try and

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.389
go save AJ.

00:07:42.389 --> 00:07:46.650
Not to mention, it's super scary to see the
Mother snarl and scream at Tess after she

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:50.000
gets hit by the car, but it doesn't keep her
down for long.

00:07:50.492 --> 00:07:55.590
The entire last act of "Barbarian" is full
of terrifying moments as AJ and Tess are in

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:57.759
a fight for their lives against the Mother.

00:07:57.759 --> 00:08:02.419
While AJ might have a moment of realization
about his behavior, that doesn't mean he's

00:08:02.419 --> 00:08:06.539
a completely different person who has magically
turned into an unselfish hero.

00:08:06.539 --> 00:08:09.360
Actually, he's the opposite of a hero as they
approach the finale.

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:14.720
By this point, AJ has accidentally shot Tess,
and he tries to sacrifice her in the final

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.520
moments of the chase just to save his skin.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:20.229
This forces the Mother to jump down and save
Tess.

00:08:20.229 --> 00:08:24.240
It's a moment that's incredibly suspenseful
since you don't know if Tess or the Mother

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:25.539
survive the fall.

00:08:25.539 --> 00:08:28.490
At first, it seems like the Mother isn't getting
back up.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:32.629
Unfortunately for AJ, she does, and she's
not letting him get away this time.

00:08:32.629 --> 00:08:37.009
AJ's death is one of the gnarliest kills of
the film as the Mother not only pokes out

00:08:37.009 --> 00:08:39.610
his eyes but crushes his head with her bare
hands.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:42.459
Director Zach Cregger doesn't hide anything
either.

00:08:42.459 --> 00:08:46.860
It's such an incredibly gory and gross kill
that's satisfying because of how terrible

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:51.269
AJ is, but it's also incredibly horrifying
because it's so graphic.

00:08:51.269 --> 00:08:53.963
No one is forgetting this kill, that's for
sure.

